This license covers everything in this repository: the software (code, styles,
pages) and the content (the Hebrew item translations, answer scales, explanations
and texts), together "the Work". It does not cover:
  - the original English items of the International Personality Item Pool (IPIP)
    and their scoring keys, which are in the public domain;
  - the items of two supplementary questionnaires that come from other
    authors' instruments: the Honesty-Humility items, several of which follow
    items of the HEXACO-PI-R (Lee & Ashton), and the ECR-RS items (Fraley et al.,
    2011). They remain subject to their authors' terms, and this license grants no
    rights in them;
  - third-party components listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, which keep their
    own licenses;
  - the name "ofiLab" and its logo (see section 6).

1. Permission
   You may use, copy, run, study and modify the Work, and share it with others,
   free of charge, for the purposes allowed in section 2 and under the
   conditions in sections 3–5.

2. Allowed purposes
   The Work is for the benefit of people, not for profit. You may use it:
   a. personally, for self-exploration;
   b. for research, study and teaching, including at schools, colleges,
      universities and courses that charge tuition, provided that the
      questionnaire, its results and its reports are not sold or charged for;
   c. in nonprofit organizations, public bodies and charities;
   d. as a professional (for example a psychologist, counselor or coach) with
      your clients, even if you are paid for your own services, provided that
      the client is not charged anything for the questionnaire, its results or
      its reports, and no fee depends on them.

3. No income
   Neither you nor anyone acting with you may receive money or any other
   compensation in connection with the Work or with any copy, version or service
   based on it. This includes, for example: fees, subscriptions, paid features or
   paid reports; advertising, sponsorship or affiliate income; donations
   requested through the Work; and selling or licensing data collected through
   it. The general funding of an organization that uses the Work for an allowed
   purpose is not affected, provided that it is not tied to the Work.

4. Restricted uses
   You may not use the Work, its results or its content:
   a. to make or inform decisions about people in employment: hiring,
      screening or selecting candidates, promotion, evaluation or dismissal.
      An employer may offer the Work to employees for voluntary
      self-exploration only if the employer does not receive or see their
      answers or results. The questionnaire is not validated for such decisions;
   b. to train, fine-tune or evaluate an artificial intelligence model that is
      offered for payment or used in a commercial product or service. Use for
      noncommercial research models is allowed under the other terms of this
      license;
   c. for any purpose that is not an allowed purpose under section 2, unless
      you have written permission from the copyright holder.

5. Conditions
   a. Credit. Every copy or version that is used by others, including a website,
      must show in a visible place (for example the footer of each page):
      "Based on ofiLab by Avraham David" with a link to
      https://ofilab.avrahamd.ovh. Keep this license and the copyright notice
      with every copy of the source.
   b. Share alike. If you make a modified version available to others in any
      way, including by running it as a website, you must make its complete
      source available to its users, free of charge, under this same license,
      and state clearly that you changed it. (A website made from the Work
      delivers its code to every visitor's browser; this condition ensures the
      code of every version stays available and readable.)
   c. No additional restrictions. You may not add terms that limit the rights
      this license gives to the people you share the Work with.

6. Name and logo
   This license does not grant any right to use the name "ofiLab", its logo, or
   any name or mark that could be confused with them. A modified or separate
   version must use its own name and branding, and must not suggest that it is
   ofiLab or endorsed by its author. The credit line in section 5a is allowed.

7. Other permissions
   Uses outside this license, including commercial uses, may be allowed by
   written permission from the copyright holder. Requests:
   https://github.com/avraham-d/OfiLab/issues

8. Ending of the license
   If you break the terms of this license, your permission ends automatically.
   If you correct the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it, and it is
